WEBVTT

00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:02.614
Of, like, what were you doing
when you were their age?

00:00:02.614 --> 00:00:05.894
And what are some of the steps
that you took from that point to

00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:09.094
where you are now to lead
you where you are today?

00:00:09.094 --> 00:00:12.374
I was doing this. Like, I literally
was sitting in a room exactly

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:15.022
like where you all are right
now on the other side of this.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.830
This room, but probably the same
room on the other side of the

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.110
building. And uh it was an
entrepreneurship class called NFTE,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.550
the network to teach
entrepreneurship.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.582
So NFTE was my first
exposure to entrepreneurship.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:28.982
It's very similar to what
Gray Matter is doing now.

00:00:28.982 --> 00:00:30.502
And I think you all
have magnified it.

00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:31.862
And that's why I'm here, right?

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:34.342
I support programs like
this wholeheartedly.

00:00:34.342 --> 00:00:36.022
But I was doing exactly
what y'all were doing:

00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:38.982
sitting around, listening to people
who've been in their profession,

00:00:38.982 --> 00:00:40.502
who are navigating life, right?

00:00:40.502 --> 00:00:42.742
Like I could get up here and act
like I'm extremely successful,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.382
but we're all navigating
where we are right now.

00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:48.742
Real time. No matter where you
are, no matter how far you've come,

00:00:48.742 --> 00:00:49.862
you're still navigating it.

00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:51.534
And I was just
trying to figure out.

00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:52.998
What was an entrepreneur?

00:00:52.998 --> 00:00:54.926
Like, I was interested
in this class.

00:00:55.014 --> 00:00:56.854
When I grew up in
Roseland as well.

00:00:56.854 --> 00:00:59.574
So, you know, I used to,
I lived right down 111th.

00:00:59.574 --> 00:01:01.518
I used to catch
111th streets here.

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:04.022
And when we used to get out of
school before basketball season

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:05.614
started, the kids
used to get beat up.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:06.834
outside the gate.

00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:09.934
all the time. And so I was
like, okay, I don't want to.

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:11.478
How do I like, what can I do?

00:01:11.478 --> 00:01:13.238
So this entrepreneurship
class was at the school.

00:01:13.238 --> 00:01:15.054
So I was like, all right, I'm
going to go to entrepreneurship.

00:01:15.622 --> 00:01:17.774
And I started taking it serious.

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:19.558
And I started asking
questions like, you know,

00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:20.278
what does this mean?

00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:21.878
How do we do this?
How do we do that?

00:01:21.878 --> 00:01:23.958
And I think at one point I
might have took the book home.

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.758
I was like, no, I told my professor
or the teacher at the time,

00:01:26.758 --> 00:01:28.046
like, I'm gonna take this book.

00:01:28.102 --> 00:01:31.302
And I just dove into it and it blew
my mind because I didn't realize

00:01:31.302 --> 00:01:33.942
that, like, everything that's
going on around you is connected

00:01:33.942 --> 00:01:35.222
to entrepreneurship, right?

00:01:35.222 --> 00:01:37.142
Like, the you know,
old-fashioned donuts,

00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:38.766
I used to walk up the
street and go there.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.150
When I knew it wasn't going to
be no squabbles at the school.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.630
And it was just something
that was like, man,

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.910
everything around me that I
experienced is some sort of a business.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.270
There's a story to be told.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.662
And that's kind of where
my curiosity sparked.

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:54.822
And then advertising was
introduced to me in college.

00:01:54.822 --> 00:01:56.732
So it started here.

00:01:56.822 --> 00:01:57.922
From here, I found a career.

00:01:59.142 --> 00:02:02.022
that then allowed me to get
back to entrepreneurship.

00:02:02.022 --> 00:02:04.768
And so I can talk to you guys
about that full circle moment.
